{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_e510bfd5a9111c26ff795db1435af5fb19e5dacb6e1e44faf0248dd9d0cd7fa2", "title": "Autosport", "text": "Autosport (ISSN 0269-946X  ) is a weekly magazine covering motorsport, published in the United Kingdom every Thursday. It was first published on 25 August 1950 by Gregor Grant, immediately prior to the Silverstone International Trophy meeting of that year. In 2016, Haymarket Media Group sold Autosport and other motorsport media outlets to Motorsport Network.", "score": 18.4904}, {"id": "hp_doc_1eb39b9821f70a66ecf6d83d3f738c1c9f262db3f585b309cf74bae47aa2cba6", "title": "Euroinvestor", "text": "Euroinvestor.com A/S is a Danish media company, operating the financial news and information website Euroinvestor as well as several additional websites and subsidiaries. Established by Søren and Jens Almindes in 1997, the company is currently majority owned by Saxo Bank, having acquired a majority stake in April 2011.", "score": 15.0333}, {"id": "hp_doc_96eff57b45d151936d0844b4b0d776152cacdc84cccad5cd844b510a6e5937a1", "title": "Dunlop Tyres", "text": "Dunlop is a brand of tyres owned by various companies around the world. Founded by pneumatic tyre pioneer John Boyd Dunlop in Birmingham, England in 1889, it is owned and operated by Goodyear Tire and Rubber Company in North America, Europe, Australia and New Zealand. In India the brand is owned by Dunlop India Ltd. whose parent company is the Ruia Group. In Asia (Japan, China, Indonesia, Thailand and Russia), Africa and Latin America (except Mexico) by Sumitomo Rubber Industries.", "score": 11.1901}], "remaining_searches": 1}
